cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RT-plm-benchmark: an honest benchmark for out-of-family reverse transcriptase activity prediction"
message: "If you use this benchmark or the search-capacity null, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Tanish"
    alias: "TanishDevs11"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TanishDevs11/RT-plm-benchmark"
abstract: >
  A methodological rebuild of an RT activity prediction submission, replacing a
  metric value that was directly optimized against its own test labels with a
  nested leave-one-family-out protocol, bootstrap intervals, and a
  search-capacity null that measures how much of any reported score a selection
  procedure can manufacture from pure noise at this sample size.
keywords:
  - protein language models
  - reverse transcriptase
  - benchmark
  - data leakage
  - small sample inference
license: MIT
